\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Heavy-tail preservation: excess kurtosis and Hill tail index vs calibrated $\beta $.} Each point is a per-ticker median over $100$ replications. \emph  {Left:} excess kurtosis, $y$-axis clipped to $[-2, 20]$ for readability. The dashed line marks the median real-data excess kurtosis across the universe ($\kappa _{\mathrm  {real}} \approx 13$); the hybrid and naive composers (orange and blue) track the generator's kurtosis, while Gaussian SIM collapses to $\kappa \approx 1$. \emph  {Right:} Hill tail-index estimator on the upper $5\%$ of $|g|$. The hybrid and naive medians sit near $0.37$ throughout the $\beta $ range; Gaussian SIM drops to $\sim 0.22$, indicating the shift toward a thinner-tailed distribution. The hybrid's median sitting below $\kappa _{\mathrm  {real}}$ reflects the JumpHMM marginal's own kurtosis rather than a composition-rule distortion; the panel's point is that hybrid tracks naive (inheriting generator tails) while Gaussian SIM does not.}}{25}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tails}{{S2}{25}{\textbf {Heavy-tail preservation: excess kurtosis and Hill tail index vs calibrated $\beta $.} Each point is a per-ticker median over $100$ replications. \emph {Left:} excess kurtosis, $y$-axis clipped to $[-2, 20]$ for readability. The dashed line marks the median real-data excess kurtosis across the universe ($\kappa _{\real } \approx 13$); the hybrid and naive composers (orange and blue) track the generator's kurtosis, while Gaussian SIM collapses to $\kappa \approx 1$. \emph {Right:} Hill tail-index estimator on the upper $5\%$ of $|g|$. The hybrid and naive medians sit near $0.37$ throughout the $\beta $ range; Gaussian SIM drops to $\sim 0.22$, indicating the shift toward a thinner-tailed distribution. The hybrid's median sitting below $\kappa _{\real }$ reflects the JumpHMM marginal's own kurtosis rather than a composition-rule distortion; the panel's point is that hybrid tracks naive (inheriting generator tails) while Gaussian SIM does not}{figure.caption.16}{}}
